      "text": "A Legends of Ren Zu excerpt, chapter four, has Ren Zu gone mad after fate Gu’s manipulation separates him from his children and after he loses wealth Gu, meeting birds, beasts, and fish who each warn him to cherish freedom Gu if he ever holds it, for they let theirs go. Freedom Gu then flies to him of its own accord, drawn by the cognition Gu on him rather than for his sake, and Ren Zu holds on to it as fate Gu’s spider silk binds him again, tearing into his bones. Once the silk eases and cognition Gu withdraws, Ren Zu asks after freedom Gu, and the moment he opens his hands in panic to look for it, it flies free and leaves him behind.",
